{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c4df","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a078cc-1760-74e1-88b8-95e63d54bb99"},"sequence":202,"recorded_at":1780531400000399,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"95ac6e07-9332-4f27-bb68-19da4362cead","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"95ac6e07-9332-4f27-bb68-19da4362cead","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"95ac6e07-9332-4f27-bb68-19da4362cead"},"call_id":"call_01a078cc77ba77a2a4d3e7a2046d39bd","text":"Read text file `internal/provhost/protocol.go`.\n(499 line(s) above)\n500|\t\t\treturn Response{}, fault\n501|\t\t}\n502|\t\treturn Response{}, failure\n503|\t}\n504|\tif _, err := scalar.ParseUUIDv7(requestID); err != nil {\n505|\t\tfailure, fault := failProtocol(\"request_id is not a UUIDv7\", \"request_id\")\n506|\t\tif fault != nil {\n507|\t\t\treturn Response{}, fault\n508|\t\t}\n509|\t\treturn Response{}, failure\n510|\t}\n511|\tif requestID != wantRequestID.String() {\n512|\t\tfailure, fault := failProtocol(\"request_id does not match the request\", \"request_id\")\n513|\t\tif fault != nil {\n514|\t\t\treturn Response{}, fault\n515|\t\t}\n516|\t\treturn Response{}, failure\n517|\t}\n518|\tif ok {\n519|\t\tif !isJSONObject(members[\"body\"]) {\n520|\t\t\tfailure, fault := failProtocol(\"body is not a JSON object\", \"body\")\n521|\t\t\tif fault != nil {\n522|\t\t\t\treturn Response{}, fault\n523|\t\t\t}\n524|\t\t\treturn Response{}, failure\n525|\t\t}\n526|\t\treturn Response{Body: append(json.RawMessage(nil), members[\"body\"]...)}, nil\n527|\t}\n528|\tif !isJSONObject(members[\"error\"]) {\n529|\t\tfailure, fault := failProtocol(\"error is not a JSON object\", \"error\")\n530|\t\tif fault != nil {\n531|\t\t\treturn Response{}, fault\n532|\t\t}\n533|\t\treturn Response{}, failure\n534|\t}\n535|\t// The failure-error version is selected by the observed envelope\n536|\t// major through the static Section 15.1/17.1 table, never from the\n537|\t// document: major 2 decodes under Structured Error 1.0.0, and major\n538|\t// 3 would decode under Structured Error 1.3.0. Only 2.0.0 reaches\n539|\t// this line — a recognizable 3.x envelope was refused above as a\n540|\t// major mismatch, because a v2-only host never trusts a different\n541|\t// major's error (Section 7.A) — so the contract below carries major\n542|\t// 2 on every reachable path today, and admits 1.3.0 by construction\n543|\t// the day the version gate admits 3.0.0. The blank parse result is\n544|\t// total here: the gate above admitted exactly \"2.0.0\".\n545|\tobservedMajor, _ := parseMajor(version)\n546|\tchild, err := axerror.DecodeBound(axerror.ContainingContract{ID: ProtocolID, Major: observedMajor}, members[\"error\"])\n547|\tif err != nil {\n548|\t\tfailure, fault := failProtocol(\"error is not a bound Structured Error 1.0.0\", \"error\")\n549|\t\tif fault != nil {\n550|\t\t\treturn Response{}, fault\n551|\t\t}\n552|\t\treturn Response{}, failure\n553|\t}\n554|\treturn Response{}, child\n555|}","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c4e1","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a078cc-1760-74e1-88b8-95e63d54bb99"},"sequence":203,"recorded_at":1780531400000401,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"95ac6e07-9332-4f27-bb68-19da4362cead","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"95ac6e07-9332-4f27-bb68-19da4362cead","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"95ac6e07-9332-4f27-bb68-19da4362cead"},"call_id":"call_01a078cc78747792830e61b238c89672","text":"Read text file `internal/provhost/identity.go`.\n1|package provhost\n2|\n3|import (\n4|\t\"encoding/json\"\n5|\t\"regexp\"\n6|\t\"strings\"\n7|\n8|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/canonicaljson\"\n9|)\n10|\n11|// This file validates the Provider Identity Record (Section 5.5,\n12|// urn:ax:schema:provider-identity 1.0.0) the host reads from\n13|// identify-session results and carries in launch, resume, quiesce,\n14|// and fork bodies, plus the identify-session success wrapper. The\n15|// record_id is required to be a digest but is not recomputed here:\n16|// content addressing belongs to the object-identity story, and this\n17|// package holds no canonical encoder. The opaque_identity absolute\n18|// prefix rule mirrors the decidable half of the Section 5.5\n19|// sentence: a value beginning with an absolute path is refused, and\n20|// an embedded path the prefix cannot see is a stated bound.\n21|//\n22|// CheckIdentity validates the record shape in this package's provider-stdio\n23|// dialect (provider_protocol_error with member attribution, which the\n24|// shared package cannot mint) and conjoins the verdict with the owner's\n25|// production identity entry canonicaljson.CalculateObjectIdentity: the two\n26|// validators must agree on the Section 5.5 shape rule for rule, and a\n27|// document the dialect admits but the owner refuses is refused at the\n28|// owner gate below. The decoder half of that agreement is pinned by the\n29|// derived TestSurrogateGateDerivedSweepAgreesWithCanonicalJSON sweep,\n30|// which judges escape and raw-UTF-8 vectors through the shared\n31|// decodeStrictObject every entry here reads through, and any shape-rule\n32|// change must land in both validators in the same change.\n33|//\n34|// Binding verification split, stated plainly: the three terminal\n35|// schemas verify their identity binding — terminalbackend's Parse\n36|// entries recompute the omit-self digest and refuse a mismatched claim\n37|// — while provider-identity records admitted here do not. CheckIdentity\n38|// requires record_id to be a well-formed digest but never recomputes\n39|// it, and the conjoined CalculateObjectIdentity entry validates shape\n40|// only; the entry that would attest the binding,\n41|// canonicaljson.VerifyObjectIdentity, is not consulted. The reason is\n42|// transport scope, not oversight: this gate validates a record embedded\n43|// in a request-correlated provider response (request_id match plus the\n44|// wantProviderID caller correlation above), and it must admit the\n45|// pinned Section 5.5 example itself, whose record_id is illustrative\n46|// rather than the true omit-self digest. Binding attestation belongs to\n47|// the identity owner at the persistence layer, through VerifyObjectIdentity.\n48|\n49|// identitySchema is the exact schema identifier the record carries.\n50|const identitySchema = \"urn:ax:schema:provider-identity\"\n51|\n52|// identitySchemaVersion is the only identity version accepted.\n53|const identitySchemaVersion = \"1.0.0\"\n54|\n55|// identityKinds is the closed identity-kind enum in section order.\n56|var identityKinds = []string{\n57|\t\"session_uuid\",\n58|\t\"session_path_or_id\",\n59|\t\"backend_conversation_uuid\",\n60|\t\"task_board_managed\",\n61|\t\"provider_defined\",\n62|}\n63|\n64|// identityMembers is the exact required member set of a Provider\n65|// Identity Record.\n66|var identityMembers = map[string]bool{\n67|\t\"schema\":                    true,\n68|\t\"schema_version\":            true,\n69|\t\"record_id\":                 true,\n70|\t\"subject_id\":                true,\n71|\t\"session_id\":                true,\n72|\t\"provider_id\":               true,\n73|\t\"provider_version\":          true,\n74|\t\"provider_version_range\":    true,\n75|\t\"native_session_id\":         true,\n76|\t\"identity_kind\":             true,\n77|\t\"logical_workspace_id\":      true,\n78|\t\"backend_realm_fingerprint\": true,\n79|\t\"opaque_identity\":           true,\n80|\t\"created_by_host_id\":        true,\n81|\t\"created_at\":                true,\n82|\t\"extensions\":                true,\n83|}\n84|\n85|// identityRequired lists identityMembers in a fixed order so a record\n86|// missing several members always names the same one.\n87|var identityRequired = []string{\n88|\t\"schema\",\n89|\t\"schema_version\",\n90|\t\"record_id\",\n91|\t\"subject_id\",\n92|\t\"session_id\",\n93|\t\"provider_id\",\n94|\t\"provider_version\",\n95|\t\"provider_version_range\",\n96|\t\"native_session_id\",\n97|\t\"identity_kind\",\n98|\t\"logical_workspace_id\",\n99|\t\"backend_realm_fingerprint\",\n100|\t\"opaque_identity\",\n101|\t\"created_by_host_id\",\n102|\t\"created_at\",\n103|\t\"extensions\",\n104|}\n105|\n106|// identityKeyPattern is the provider-identity key grammar Section 5.5\n107|// states: [a-z][a-z0-9_.-]{0,63}.\n108|var identityKeyPattern = regexp.MustCompile(`^[a-z][a-z0-9_.-]{0,63}$`)\n109|\n110|// windowsDrivePattern matches a Windows drive-qualified absolute\n111|// prefix: a letter, a colon, and a separator.\n112|var windowsDrivePattern = regexp.MustCompile(`^[A-Za-z]:[\\\\/]`)\n113|\n114|// CheckIdentity validates one Provider Identity Record naming the\n115|// expected provider. Shape violations are provider_protocol_errors;\n116|// a well-formed record for another provider is an invalid_config\n117|// caller error: the caller correlated the wrong identity to this\n118|// session.\n119|func CheckIdentity(body []byte, wantProviderID string) error {\n120|\tmembers, fault := decodeStrictObject(body)\n121|\tif fault != nil {\n122|\t\tfailure, err := failProtocol(fault.detail, fault.member)\n123|\t\tif err != nil {\n124|\t\t\treturn err\n125|\t\t}\n126|\t\treturn failure\n127|\t}\n128|\tif name, unknown := unknownMember(members, identityMembers); unknown {\n129|\t\tfailure, err := failProtocol(\"identity carries unknown member\", name)\n130|\t\tif err != nil {\n131|\t\t\treturn err\n132|\t\t}\n133|\t\treturn failure\n134|\t}\n135|\tif name, missing := missingMember(members, identityRequired); missing {\n136|\t\tfailure, err := failProtocol(\"identity misses a required member\", name)\n137|\t\tif err != nil {\n138|\t\t\treturn err\n139|\t\t}\n140|\t\treturn failure\n141|\t}\n142|\tif schema, ok := rawString(members[\"schema\"]); !ok || schema != identitySchema {\n143|\t\tfailure, err := failProtocol(\"identity schema is not the provider identity\", \"schema\")\n144|\t\tif err != nil {\n145|\t\t\treturn err\n146|\t\t}\n147|\t\treturn failure\n148|\t}\n149|\tif version, ok := rawString(members[\"schema_version\"]); !ok || version != identitySchemaVersion {\n150|\t\tfailure, err := failProtocol(\"identity schema_version is not 1.0.0\", \"schema_version\")\n151|\t\tif err != nil {\n152|\t\t\treturn err\n153|\t\t}\n154|\t\treturn failure\n155|\t}\n156|\tif digest, ok := rawString(members[\"record_id\"]); !ok || !isDigest(digest) {\n157|\t\tfailure, err := failProtocol(\"identity record_id is not a digest\", \"record_id\")\n158|\t\tif err != nil {\n159|\t\t\treturn err\n160|\t\t}\n161|\t\treturn failure\n162|\t}\n163|\tsubject, ok := rawString(members[\"subject_id\"])\n164|\tif !ok || !isUUIDv7(subject) {\n165|\t\tfailure, err := failProtocol(\"identity subject_id is not a UUIDv7\", \"subject_id\")\n166|\t\tif err != nil {\n167|\t\t\treturn err\n168|\t\t}\n169|\t\treturn failure\n170|\t}\n171|\tsession, ok := rawString(members[\"session_id\"])\n172|\tif !ok || !isUUIDv7(session) {\n173|\t\tfailure, err := failProtocol(\"identity session_id is not a UUIDv7\", \"session_id\")\n174|\t\tif err != nil {\n175|\t\t\treturn err\n176|\t\t}\n177|\t\treturn failure\n178|\t}\n179|\tif subject != session {\n180|\t\tfailure, err := failProtocol(\"identity subject_id does not equal session_id\", \"subject_id\")\n181|\t\tif err != nil {\n182|\t\t\treturn err\n183|\t\t}\n184|\t\treturn failure\n185|\t}\n186|\tprovider, ok := rawString(members[\"provider_id\"])\n187|\tif !ok || !validProviderID(provider) {\n188|\t\tfailure, err := failProtocol(\"identity provider_id is not a provider id\", \"provider_id\")\n189|\t\tif err != nil {\n190|\t\t\treturn err\n191|\t\t}\n192|\t\treturn failure\n193|\t}\n194|\tif provider != wantProviderID {\n195|\t\tfailure, err := failInvalid(\"identity names another provider\")\n196|\t\tif err != nil {\n197|\t\t\treturn err\n198|\t\t}\n199|\t\treturn failure\n200|\t}\n201|\tif !isBoundedString(members[\"provider_version\"], 1, 128) {\n202|\t\tfailure, err := failProtocol(\"identity provider_version is not 1..128 characters\", \"provider_version\")\n203|\t\tif err != nil {\n204|\t\t\treturn err\n205|\t\t}\n206|\t\treturn failure\n207|\t}\n208|\tif !isBoundedString(members[\"provider_version_range\"], 1, 256) {\n209|\t\tfailure, err := failProtocol(\"identity provider_version_range is not 1..256 characters\", \"provider_version_range\")\n210|\t\tif err != nil {\n211|\t\t\treturn err\n212|\t\t}\n213|\t\treturn failure\n214|\t}\n215|\tif !isBoundedString(members[\"native_session_id\"], 1, 512) {\n216|\t\tfailure, err := failProtocol(\"identity native_session_id is not 1..512 characters\", \"native_session_id\")\n217|\t\tif err != nil {\n218|\t\t\treturn err\n219|\t\t}\n220|\t\treturn failure\n221|\t}\n222|\tkind, ok := rawString(members[\"identity_kind\"])\n223|\tif !ok || !isIdentityKind(kind) {\n224|\t\tfailure, err := failProtocol(\"identity kind is not a registry member\", \"identity_kind\")\n225|\t\tif err != nil {\n226|\t\t\treturn err\n227|\t\t}\n228|\t\treturn failure\n229|\t}\n230|\tif workspace, ok := rawString(members[\"logical_workspace_id\"]); !ok || !isUUIDv7(workspace) {\n231|\t\tfailure, err := failProtocol(\"identity workspace is not a UUIDv7\", \"logical_workspace_id\")\n232|\t\tif err != nil {\n233|\t\t\treturn err\n234|\t\t}\n235|\t\treturn failure\n236|\t}\n237|\tif err := checkIdentityRealm(members[\"backend_realm_fingerprint\"], provider, kind); err != nil {\n238|\t\treturn err\n239|\t}\n240|\tif err := checkIdentityOpaque(members[\"opaque_identity\"]); err != nil {\n241|\t\treturn err\n242|\t}\n243|\tif host, ok := rawString(members[\"created_by_host_id\"]); !ok || !isUUIDv7(host) {\n244|\t\tfailure, err := failProtocol(\"identity host is not a UUIDv7\", \"created_by_host_id\")\n245|\t\tif err != nil {\n246|\t\t\treturn err\n247|\t\t}\n248|\t\treturn failure\n249|\t}\n250|\tif created, ok := rawString(members[\"created_at\"]); !ok || !isTimestamp(created) {\n251|\t\tfailure, err := failProtocol(\"identity timestamp is not a timestamp\", \"created_at\")\n252|\t\tif err != nil {\n253|\t\t\treturn err\n254|\t\t}\n255|\t\treturn failure\n256|\t}\n257|\tif !isJSONObject(members[\"extensions\"]) {\n258|\t\tfailure, err := failProtocol(\"identity extensions is not an object\", \"extensions\")\n259|\t\tif err != nil {\n260|\t\t\treturn err\n261|\t\t}\n262|\t\treturn failure\n263|\t}\n264|\t// The member arms above are this package's provider-stdio dialect of\n265|\t// the Section 5.5 rule; the owner of that rule is canonicaljson\n266|\t// (validateProviderIdentityRecord, registered for section:5.5 in the\n267|\t// traceability registry), and the dialect keeps its member attribution\n268|\t// deliberately. The verdict is therefore conjoined with the owner's\n269|\t// production identity entry: a document this dialect admits but the\n270|\t// owner refuses — open extensions content, a number the dialect never\n271|\t// reads, nesting beyond the dialect's view — is refused here rather\n272|\t// than admitted through a drifted copy. The provider-equality\n273|\t// correlation above stays host-side: it is a caller rule, not a\n274|\t// content rule, and the owner never sees it.\n275|\tif _, _, err := canonicaljson.CalculateObjectIdentity(body); err != nil {\n276|\t\tfailure, ferr := failProtocol(\"identity is not a valid provider identity\", \"\")\n277|\t\tif ferr != nil {\n278|\t\t\treturn ferr\n279|\t\t}\n280|\t\treturn failure\n281|\t}\n282|\treturn nil\n283|}\n284|\n285|// checkIdentityRealm enforces the digest-or-null shape and the one\n286|// conditional rule Section 5.5 states: an Antigravity\n287|// backend_conversation_uuid MUST carry a non-null realm fingerprint,\n288|// because the backend realm is a resume precondition there.\n289|func checkIdentityRealm(raw json.RawMessage, provider, kind string) error {\n290|\trealm, isNull, ok := rawNullableString(raw)\n291|\tif !ok || (!isNull && !isDigest(realm)) {\n292|\t\tfailure, err := failProtocol(\"identity realm is not a digest or null\", \"backend_realm_fingerprint\")\n293|\t\tif err != nil {\n294|\t\t\treturn err\n295|\t\t}\n296|\t\treturn failure\n297|\t}\n298|\tif provider == \"antigravity\" && kind == \"backend_conversation_uuid\" && isNull {\n299|\t\tfailure, err := failProtocol(\"identity realm is required for this backend kind\", \"backend_realm_fingerprint\")\n300|\t\tif err != nil {\n301|\t\t\treturn err\n302|\t\t}\n303|\t\treturn failure\n304|\t}\n305|\treturn nil\n306|}\n307|\n308|// checkIdentityOpaque enforces the explicit adapter-data surface: an\n309|// object of at most 32 entries, keyed by the provider-identity key\n310|// grammar, with non-secret string values of 1..1,024 characters that\n311|// MUST NOT begin with an absolute path.\n312|func checkIdentityOpaque(raw json.RawMessage) error {\n313|\topaque, fault := decodeStrictObject(raw)\n314|\tif fault != nil {\n315|\t\tfailure, err := failProtocol(fault.detail, fault.member)\n316|\t\tif err != nil {\n317|\t\t\treturn err\n318|\t\t}\n319|\t\treturn failure\n320|\t}\n321|\tif len(opaque) > 32 {\n322|\t\tfailure, err := failProtocol(\"identity opaque_identity exceeds 32 entries\", \"opaque_identity\")\n323|\t\tif err != nil {\n324|\t\t\treturn err\n325|\t\t}\n326|\t\treturn failure\n327|\t}\n328|\tkeys := make([]string, 0, len(opaque))\n329|\tfor key := range opaque {\n330|\t\tkeys = append(keys, key)\n331|\t}\n332|\tfor _, key := range keys {\n333|\t\tif !identityKeyPattern.MatchString(key) {\n334|\t\t\tfailure, err := failProtocol(\"identity opaque key is not a provider key\", \"opaque_identity\")\n335|\t\t\tif err != nil {\n336|\t\t\t\treturn err\n337|\t\t\t}\n338|\t\t\treturn failure\n339|\t\t}\n340|\t\tvalue, ok := rawString(opaque[key])\n341|\t\tif !ok || runeLength(value) < 1 || runeLength(value) > 1024 {\n342|\t\t\tfailure, err := failProtocol(\"identity opaque value is not 1..1024 characters\", \"opaque_identity\")\n343|\t\t\tif err != nil {\n344|\t\t\t\treturn err\n345|\t\t\t}\n346|\t\t\treturn failure\n347|\t\t}\n348|\t\tif strings.HasPrefix(value, \"/\") || strings.HasPrefix(value, `\\\\`) || windowsDrivePattern.MatchString(value) {\n349|\t\t\tfailure, err := failProtocol(\"identity opaque value begins with an absolute path\", \"opaque_identity\")\n350|\t\t\tif err != nil {\n351|\t\t\t\treturn err\n352|\t\t\t}\n353|\t\t\treturn failure\n354|\t\t}\n355|\t}\n356|\treturn nil\n357|}\n358|\n359|func isIdentityKind(value string) bool {\n360|\tfor _, kind := range identityKinds {\n361|\t\tif value == kind {\n362|\t\t\treturn true\n363|\t\t}\n364|\t}\n365|\treturn false\n366|}\n367|\n368|// identifyMembers is the exact required member set of an\n369|// identify-session success body.\n370|var identifyMembers = map[string]bool{\n371|\t\"identity\":         true,\n372|\t\"confidence\":       true,\n373|\t\"matched_evidence\": true,\n374|}\n375|\n376|// identifyRequired lists identifyMembers in a fixed order.\n377|var identifyRequired = []string{\"identity\", \"confidence\", \"matched_evidence\"}\n378|\n379|// identifyConfidences is the closed confidence vocabulary.\n380|var identifyConfidences = []string{\"exact\", \"strong\", \"weak\"}\n381|\n382|// identifyEvidence is the closed matched-evidence vocabulary.\n383|var identifyEvidence = []string{\"native_id\", \"store_path\", \"provider_event\", \"backend_lookup\"}\n384|\n385|// DecodeIdentifyResult validates one identify-session success body:\n386|// the Provider Identity Record for the expected provider, a closed\n387|// confidence, and 1..4 sorted unique matched-evidence members.\n388|func DecodeIdentifyResult(body []byte, wantProviderID string) error {\n389|\tmembers, fault := decodeStrictObject(body)\n390|\tif fault != nil {\n391|\t\tfailure, err := failProtocol(fault.detail, fault.member)\n392|\t\tif err != nil {\n393|\t\t\treturn err\n394|\t\t}\n395|\t\treturn failure\n396|\t}\n397|\tif name, unknown := unknownMember(members, identifyMembers); unknown {\n398|\t\tfailure, err := failProtocol(\"identify result carries unknown member\", name)\n399|\t\tif err != nil {\n400|\t\t\treturn err\n401|\t\t}\n402|\t\treturn failure\n403|\t}\n404|\tif name, missing := missingMember(members, identifyRequired); missing {\n405|\t\tfailure, err := failProtocol(\"identify result misses a required member\", name)\n406|\t\tif err != nil {\n407|\t\t\treturn err\n408|\t\t}\n409|\t\treturn failure\n410|\t}\n411|\tconfidence, ok := rawString(members[\"confidence\"])\n412|\tif !ok || !isIdentifyConfidence(confidence) {\n413|\t\tfailure, err := failProtocol(\"identify confidence is not exact strong or weak\", \"confidence\")\n414|\t\tif err != nil {\n415|\t\t\treturn err\n416|\t\t}\n417|\t\treturn failure\n418|\t}\n419|\tif err := checkIdentifyEvidence(members[\"matched_evidence\"]); err != nil {\n420|\t\treturn err\n421|\t}\n422|\tif !isJSONObject(members[\"identity\"]) {\n423|\t\tfailure, err := failProtocol(\"identify identity is not an object\", \"identity\")\n424|\t\tif err != nil {\n425|\t\t\treturn err\n426|\t\t}\n427|\t\treturn failure\n428|\t}\n429|\tif err := CheckIdentity(members[\"identity\"], wantProviderID); err != nil {\n430|\t\treturn err\n431|\t}\n432|\treturn nil\n433|}\n434|\n435|func isIdentifyConfidence(value string) bool {\n436|\tfor _, confidence := range identifyConfidences {\n437|\t\tif value == confidence {\n438|\t\t\treturn true\n439|\t\t}\n440|\t}\n441|\treturn false\n442|}\n443|\n444|// checkIdentifyEvidence requires 1..4 sorted unique closed-vocabulary\n445|// evidence members: the observation must cite what matched, exactly\n446|// once each.\n447|func checkIdentifyEvidence(raw json.RawMessage) error {\n448|\tevidence, ok := rawStringArray(raw)\n449|\tif !ok || len(evidence) < 1 || len(evidence) > 4 {\n450|\t\tfailure, err := failProtocol(\"identify evidence is not 1..4 members\", \"matched_evidence\")\n451|\t\tif err != nil {\n452|\t\t\treturn err\n453|\t\t}\n454|\t\treturn failure\n455|\t}\n456|\tallowed := map[string]bool{}\n457|\tfor _, member := range identifyEvidence {\n458|\t\tallowed[member] = true\n459|\t}\n460|\tfor _, member := range evidence {\n461|\t\tif !allowed[member] {\n462|\t\t\tfailure, err := failProtocol(\"identify evidence names an unknown member\", \"matched_evidence\")\n463|\t\t\tif err != nil {\n464|\t\t\t\treturn err\n465|\t\t\t}\n466|\t\t\treturn failure\n467|\t\t}\n468|\t}\n469|\tif !sortedUniqueStrings(evidence) {\n470|\t\tfailure, err := failProtocol(\"identify evidence is not sorted unique\", \"matched_evidence\")\n471|\t\tif err != nil {\n472|\t\t\treturn err\n473|\t\t}\n474|\t\treturn failure\n475|\t}\n476|\treturn nil\n477|}","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c4e3","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a078cc-1760-74e1-88b8-95e63d54bb99"},"sequence":204,"recorded_at":1780531400000403,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"95ac6e07-9332-4f27-bb68-19da4362cead","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"95ac6e07-9332-4f27-bb68-19da4362cead","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"95ac6e07-9332-4f27-bb68-19da4362cead"},"call_id":"call_01a078cc78ec79c39b23c3d04c6908f7","text":"Read text file `internal/provhost/doc.go`.\n1|// Package provhost implements the ax host side of the provider plugin\n2|// JSON-over-stdio protocol of pinned specification Section 7.2: one-frame\n3|// JSONL transport, deadlines, size limits, stdout/stderr separation,\n4|// operation dispatch, and status recovery.\n5|//\n6|// The actor every Section 7.2 RFC 2119 keyword governs here is the ax host\n7|// (this repository). The provider plugin is a child process this package\n8|// starts but never trusts: every byte it emits is attacker-influenced, so\n9|// every frame is validated before any member is used, and a different-major\n10|// payload is never parsed far enough to trust its error code, retryable\n11|// bit, details, or authority fields (Section 15.1).\n12|//\n13|// This package owns the envelope layer and the operation-layer\n14|// conformance decoders. Operation dispatch means the host maps an\n15|// operation name to one plugin invocation and refuses unknown names\n16|// locally without spawning; the conformance decoders validate what a\n17|// plugin returned: the closed manifest (7.3), probe and capability\n18|// gate (7.4, 8.3), profile mapping (7.7), quiescence proof (7.6),\n19|// SpawnPlan success bodies for launch and resume, the Provider\n20|// Identity Record and identify-session result (5.5), and the single\n21|// (operation, operation_id) mutation key (7.5). Full Section 7.5\n22|// request-body vocabularies beyond these surfaces, and the\n23|// materialize commit/rollback result bodies, cross this package\n24|// opaquely: a body must still be a JSON object, and the\n25|// materialize-status body this package interprets for recovery must\n26|// satisfy the state/nullability/identity rules Section 7.5 states\n27|// for ProviderTransactionStatus.\n28|//\n29|// A failed read is never an absence: a crashed, timed-out, oversized,\n30|// unparsable, or correlation-mismatched invocation fails with a local\n31|// Structured Error 1.0.0, never with a partial response the caller could\n32|// mistake for a result. Status recovery is fail-closed the same way: an\n33|// unknown or integrity-invalid transaction fails with integrity_failure\n34|// and must be quarantined rather than represented as a successful status.\n35|//\n36|// The package mutates no durable state of its own and keeps no cross-call\n37|// cache: Host starts one plugin process per operation, so successive calls\n38|// are separate processes observing durable state through the authority the\n39|// caller passes, which is the property the cross-process recovery cases\n40|// rest on. Retry decisions belong to the caller; every local failure this\n41|// package emits is non-retryable, because nothing observed at an unusable\n42|// frame licenses a safe-retry claim.\n43|//\n44|// Stated bounds: stderr capture is capped at 1 MiB (an implementation\n45|// resource bound, not a protocol limit); error details carry the failure\n46|// class, member names, and the observed version string only — never\n47|// environment or stderr content. Mutation receipts live in the\n48|// provider transaction document and the plugin, not in the host: the\n49|// host holds no cross-call cache, so cross-crash durability of\n50|// (operation, operation_id) results is the document's property, and\n51|// the host side pins the sole key shape, byte-identical retry bytes,\n52|// and the mismatch surface. The Section 8 provider/platform cell\n53|// values are evidence labels, not host behavior: the host pins the\n54|// fail-closed direction (conditional, unsupported, and unknown are\n55|// never usable) for every capability-by-status tuple rather than one\n56|// cell value. Section 8.2 store-exclusion roots and the remaining\n57|// Section 7.5 request vocabularies have no host production yet.\n58|//\n59|// Provider Protocol 3.0.0 (§7.A), which the v0.5.0 catalog pins\n60|// alongside 2.0.0, is owned by internal/terminalbackend, not by this\n61|// package: the v3-specific production rule — parsing the closed v3\n62|// TerminalDescriptor and matching it against the AX-validated\n63|// host-local binding before a provider process is launched or observed\n64|// — is terminalbackend.AdmitProviderDescriptor, and the traceability\n65|// registry records section 7.A against terminalbackend for it. This\n66|// host speaks major 2 only: it classifies any recognizable 3.x\n67|// envelope as incompatible_protocol without trusting its payload,\n68|// which is the Section 7.A v2/v3 major-mismatch outcome (a v2/v3\n69|// mismatch follows the Section 15.1 close/termination rule; the caller\n70|// never trusts a different major's error), and any other unusable\n71|// frame as provider_protocol_error. A v3 plugin is therefore refused\n72|// loudly rather than misread as v2. The failure-error version is still\n73|// selected by the observed major, never the document: major 2 decodes\n74|// under Structured Error 1.0.0 and major 3 would decode under 1.3.0\n75|// (axerror.BindingFor), but no 3.x envelope reaches the decoder while\n76|// this host writes v2 requests. Sending v3 requests, carrying v3\n77|// descriptors in launch/resume bodies, and decoding v3 failures under\n78|// Error 1.3.0 is the dual-stack host follow-up described in this\n79|// task's outcome; until it exists, the 1.3.0 binding is named here\n80|// and implemented in axerror, not silently defaulted to 1.0.0.\n81|package provhost","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
