{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000ca77","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a078cc-1760-74e1-88b8-95e63d54bb99"},"sequence":918,"recorded_at":1780531400001831,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"95ac6e07-9332-4f27-bb68-19da4362cead","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"95ac6e07-9332-4f27-bb68-19da4362cead","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"95ac6e07-9332-4f27-bb68-19da4362cead"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"749fbcbc-2358-41d2-b24e-b213c99d68ff"},"task_id":"749fbcbc-2358-41d2-b24e-b213c99d68ff","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"749fbcbc-2358-41d2-b24e-b213c99d68ff","chunk":"Read text file `/tmp/round1_outcome.md`.\n1|# TASK-260906-vmzk0y — own-provider-protocol-v3-envelope-and-error-lift\n2|\n3|Status: ready for review (handed off to review; board status `to-review`).\n4|\n5|Candidate tree: `c027830980c32c1a90e823ebf1e101ba096af821`\n6|(verified by `git ls-tree -r`: holds all 12 changed paths; blob hash of\n7|`internal/provider/lift.go` equals the worktree bytes exactly. Built via a\n8|detached index so the worktree index is untouched. Note: `git stash create -u`\n9|was tried first and its tree omits untracked files — the recorded OID above\n10|is the detached-index tree, which holds them.)\n11|\n12|## Decision (A3): the §7.A owner is terminalbackend\n13|\n14|Provider Protocol 3.0.0 (§7.A) keeps the exact v2 framing and replaces the\n15|v2 TerminalDescriptor with one closed v3 object. The only v3-specific\n16|production decision point — parse the closed descriptor, match binding\n17|digest / backend ID+version / generation against the AX-validated\n18|host-local binding before launch or observation — now lives in\n19|`internal/terminalbackend` as `AdmitProviderDescriptor` (complete gate)\n20|over `ParseProviderDescriptor` (closed-shape front door) and the\n21|pre-existing `CheckProviderDescriptor` (match rule, unchanged). Recorded in\n22|`internal/provhost/doc.go` stated bounds and in the traceability registry\n23|(`section:7.A` → `terminalbackend/descriptor.go` `AdmitProviderDescriptor`,\n24|acceptance `terminal-provider-descriptor-7a`, digest re-pinned, `tracecheck`\n25|green).\n26|\n27|Why not provhost admission: our host writes v2 requests, and §7.A orders\n28|that \"a v2/v3 major mismatch follows the Section 15.1 close/termination\n29|rule; the caller never trusts a different major's error\". Admitting a 3.0.0\n30|response to a 2.0.0 request would trust a mismatched major and would redden\n31|the green gates pinning `3.0.0 → incompatible_protocol`\n32|(`TestDecodeResponseRecognizableMajorMismatch`,\n33|`TestDecodeResponseForeignMajorPrecedesMemberRules`). Refusal at provhost is\n34|the specified outcome, not a gap. Sending v3 requests, carrying v3\n35|descriptors in launch/resume bodies, and decoding v3 failures under Error\n36|1.3.0 is the dual-stack-host follow-up specified below; no board element\n37|was created for it (board-element freeze while the story's final leaf is\n38|open — see task brief).\n39|\n40|## AC row coverage: 11 of 11 driven\n41|\n42|| # | AC / DoD row | Production call site | Driving test |\n43||---|---|---|---|\n44|| 1 | v3 envelope has exactly one named owner, recorded in provhost stated bounds and the ownership registry | `internal/provhost/doc.go` (bounds prose), `ownership.v0.5.0.json` `section:7.A` | `tracecheck` (production gate over the registry): ok |\n45|| 2 | working v3 admission or explicit stated bound naming the deferral | `terminalbackend.AdmitProviderDescriptor` (admission); `provhost/doc.go` (transport deferral + follow-up below) | `TestAdmitProviderDescriptorAdmitsMatchingBinding`, `TestAdmitProviderDescriptorRefusesMismatch` |\n46|| 3 | v3 envelope reaching provhost → documented outcome, both directions | `provhost.DecodeResponse` (refuse); `terminalbackend.AdmitProviderDescriptor` (admit) | `TestDecodeResponseWellFormedV3SuccessIsMismatch`, `TestDecodeResponseV3FailureWithValid130ErrorIsMismatch`, admit tests above |\n47|| 4 | Error 1.3.0 binding implemented-or-deferred; no silent major-2 binding for v3 | `provhost.DecodeResponse` (contract derived from observed major), `axerror.BindingFor` (table) | `TestDecodeResponseV2FailureWith130ErrorIsBoundTo100`; 1.3.0 payload proven well-formed via `axerror.Decode(Version130, …)` probe |\n48|| 5 | discovery failure lifts into an axerror Structured Error through an accepted production path | `provider.Lift` (new, `internal/provider/lift.go`) | `TestLiftCarriesDiscoveryFailuresToTheWire` (4 real-failure vectors) |\n49|| 6 | causal-leak shape refused (negative) | `axerror.New` (production gate) | `TestNaiveLiftShapeIsRefusedByTheWireGate` (message + details directions) |\n50|| 7 | no machine-local path, provider ID, or owner identity on any wire message | `provider.Lift`, `terminalbackend` parse arms | wire-absence asserts in all 4 lift vectors (secrets first proven present locally); `TestParseProviderDescriptorRefusesWithoutEchoingLocalData` |\n51|| 8 | CheckProviderDescriptor completed; registry owns 7.A | `terminalbackend.ParseProviderDescriptor` + `AdmitProviderDescriptor`; registry | 11 new inventory arms + rows; `tracecheck` ok |\n52|| 9 | F3 binding split resolved or stated | `provhost/identity.go` header | prose by nature (states which schemas verify binding and why); terminal-side claim verified in `terminalbackend/manifest.go` `checkIdentity` |\n53|| 10 | census/inventory discipline with planted controls | derivation tests | provider `TestLiftCoversTheClosedCodeSet` (AST-derived codes + bogus-code refusal); terminalbackend 11 rows (bijection both directions) |\n54|| 11 | mutation battery with narrowing / arm-deletion / census-only split | battery scripts `/tmp/mutbattery.sh`, `/tmp/mutbattery2.sh` | table below; 17 applied, 17 killed, 0 survivors |\n55|\n56|## Production changes (12 paths)\n57|\n58|- `internal/terminalbackend/descriptor.go` (new): `ProviderDescriptor`\n59|  (9-member closed §7.A object), `ParseProviderDescriptor` (strict decode,\n60|  closed member set, per-member §7.A constraints, static details only),\n61|  `AdmitProviderDescriptor` (parse + project + `CheckProviderDescriptor`).\n62|- `internal/terminalbackend/descriptor_test.go` (new): admit, member-set\n63|  (extra/missing/duplicate), member-type sweep, value table incl. the\n64|  major-2 narrowing shape, geometry bounds, no-echo, mismatch arms.\n65|- `internal/terminalbackend/refusal_arm_inventory_test.go`: 11 declared\n66|  rows for the new arms (bijection holds both directions).\n67|- `internal/provider/lift.go` (new): `Lift` — static message per stable\n68|  code, empty details, local cause preserved for `errors.Is/As`,\n69|  fail-closed through the axerror registry for unknown codes. Builds no\n70|  refusal of its own (provider inventory untouched by construction: no\n71|  `Error` literal, no `errors.New`/`fmt.Errorf`/`panic`).\n72|- `internal/provider/lift_test.go` (new): real-lift vectors, naive-shape\n73|  refusal, AST-derived code totality.\n74|- `internal/provider/doc.go`: composition contract now names `Lift` as\n75|  the single production call site (replaces \"no such call site exists\").\n76|- `internal/provhost/protocol.go`: `providerContract` static var replaced\n77|  by a contract derived from the observed envelope major, with the\n78|  v3→1.3.0 binding named in the comment. Zero inventory delta (same\n79|  refusal sites, same literals).\n80|- `internal/provhost/protocol_test.go`: well-formed 3.0.0 success refused;\n81|  3.0.0 failure carrying a proven-well-formed 1.3.0 error refused\n82|  without trusting (full rendering asserted); 1.3.0 error under a 2.0.0\n83|  envelope refused as unbound under 1.0.0.\n84|- `internal/provhost/doc.go`: stated bounds name terminalbackend as the\n85|  §7.A owner, the v2-only mismatch rule, the named 1.3.0 binding, and the\n86|  dual-stack deferral.\n87|- `internal/provhost/identity.go`: F3 split stated plainly (terminal\n88|  schemas verify binding via recompute; provider-identity records are\n89|  shape + digest-grammar at this gate because the gate must admit the\n90|  pinned §5.5 example, whose `record_id` is illustrative; attestation\n91|  belongs to `canonicaljson.VerifyObjectIdentity` at the persistence\n92|  layer).\n93|- `internal/traceability/ownership.v0.5.0.json` + `traceability.go`:\n94|  7.A → terminalbackend, acceptance extended, digest re-pinned\n95|  (`caaca4c9…`).\n96|\n97|Leaf-1 production code untouched (`git diff HEAD --stat` shows none of\n98|leaf 1's files except the required registry/digest and test-table rows;\n99|`terminalbackend/manifest.go`, `canonicaljson/*`, `environ/*` unmodified).\n100|\n101|## Mutation battery: 17 applied, 17 killed, 0 survivors\n102|\n103|Denominator production-derived (new arms + touched gates). NOT_APPLIED\n104|and COMPILE_FAIL reported as distinct rows (controls M10/M11).\n105|\n106|| Mutant | Class | What it narrows / removes | Named failing test |\n107||---|---|---|---|\n108|| M1 proto major-1 rule dropped | narrowing | admits `protocol_version: 2.0.0` | `TestParseProviderDescriptorValueRefusals/protocol_version_major_2` (\"got admission\") |\n109|| M2 geometry bound 1000→1001 | narrowing | admits columns 1001 | `ValueRefusals/columns_over_bound` (\"got admission\") |\n110|| M3 member-set count half dropped | narrowing | admits extra member | `TestParseProviderDescriptorMemberSet` + inventory bijection (co-kill) |\n111|| M4 digest-shape arm deleted | arm-deletion | malformed digest admitted by Parse (match arm still refuses at Admit — layered) | `ValueRefusals` digest rows + `…RefusesWithoutEchoingLocalData` (\"got admission\") + inventory (co-kill) |\n112|| M5 lift carries local detail on wire | narrowing | `details: {detail: failure.detail}` | `TestLiftCarriesDiscoveryFailuresToTheWire` (`lifted details = [detail]`) |\n113|| M6 integrity arm dropped from lift switch | arm-deletion | integrity failures fail at