lity passes — proves the harness runs behavior, not only the checker |\n127|\n128|Survivors: none — no survivor bounds to state.\n129|\n130|## Gate evidence (exit codes observed in this turn)\n131|\n132|- `go test ./... -count=1`: exit 0, 22 packages ok, 0 FAIL.\n133|- `go test -race ./... -count=1`: exit 0, 22 ok.\n134|- `go test ./... -cover -count=1`: exit 0 (provhost 85.8%, provider 97.7%, terminalbackend 94.2%).\n135|- `go vet ./...`: exit 0. `GOOS=windows go vet ./...`: exit 0.\n136|- `gofmt -l internal/`: clean. `go build ./...` + `GOOS=windows go build ./...`: exit 0.\n137|- `go generate ./internal/catalog` + `git diff --exit-code`: current.\n138|- `go run ./internal/traceability/cmd/tracecheck`: ok (60 contracts, 98 acceptance cases).\n139|- cigate contract gates + claims/targets selections: exit 0.\n140|- Not run: fuzz smoke — targets live in `secconftest`/`canonicaljson`/`scalar`, none touched and none listed in the touched packages; CI runs it.\n141|\n142|## Follow-up: dual-stack v3 host (deferring task content)\n143|\n144|No board element was created (freeze while the story's final leaf is open).\n145|Proposed task: implement the dual-stack provider host — negotiate/send v3\n146|requests per plugin, carry the §7.A descriptor (built via\n147|`ParseProviderDescriptor`) in v3 launch/resume bodies, decode v3 failures\n148|under Structured Error 1.3.0 through the major-derived contract in\n149|`provhost.DecodeResponse`, and refuse non-`ax.tmux`/`ax.conpty` backends as\n150|`incompatible_protocol` per §7.A/§4.E (no fallback). Acceptance: v3 request\n151|bytes on the wire, 1.3.0 failure decode under test, descriptor mismatch\n152|refused before launch through `AdmitProviderDescriptor` from a real call\n153|path. Until then the stated bounds above govern."}}}
