 the outcome, not a silent scope.\\n+- DECISION: `provider.Error` keeps machine-local facts for logs; the wire message is rebuilt from the stable code alone by `Lift` (static text, empty details, cause local-only). Constructor restructuring would not remove the rebuild need, so the seam is the lift, documented in `provider/doc.go`.\\n+- FINDING: `git stash create -u` trees omit untracked files — verify candidate trees with `git ls-tree`. The recorded tree OID was built via a detached index (`GIT_INDEX_FILE` copy + `add -A` + `write-tree`) with blob hashes checked against worktree bytes.\\n+- EVIDENCE: outcome `TASK-260906-vmzk0y_outcome.md` on the board task (11/11 AC rows with call sites, 19-row mutant table, gates with exit codes, candidate tree OID verified by `ls-tree`).\\n+- GATES: `go test ./... -count=1` exit 0 (22 pkgs), `-race` exit 0, `-cover` exit 0, `go vet` + `GOOS=windows go vet/build` exit 0, gofmt clean, catalog current, `tracecheck` ok. Battery 17 applied / 17 killed / 0 survivors (+ NOT_APPLIED and COMPILE_FAIL controls). Fuzz smoke not run (targets in untouched packages; CI runs it).\\n+- STATUS: Ready for review, handed off to review (review/integration are orchestrator steps).\\n+\\n ### 2249 — CI gates leaf round 2: five review findings closed, all claims reproduce\\n - SCOPE: TASK-260830-2uowwk rework (review-verdict-rev1, F1–F5 blocking + verb-battery observation). `internal/cigate` + `.github/workflows/ci.yml` + README. `internal/secprim` + `internal/secconftest` production untouched (restored byte-identical after two probe mutants; `git status` clean on both).\\n - F1: deleted the `Record live probe verdicts` step — it ran a synthetic-verdict test and grepped a constant line through a non-gating pipe. CI now scans the README with every probe forced unavailable (stronger than live scanning, host-independent); README table and `cigate/doc.go` say so, and the workflow comment states `ProbeState.Available` is consumed by no call site.\\n\",\n  