{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000d3dd","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a078cc-1760-74e1-88b8-95e63d54bb99"},"sequence":2121,"recorded_at":1780531400004237,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"95ac6e07-9332-4f27-bb68-19da4362cead","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"95ac6e07-9332-4f27-bb68-19da4362cead","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"95ac6e07-9332-4f27-bb68-19da4362cead"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"4f378b3f-6686-4d4d-a7d7-9f681fba3170"},"task_id":"4f378b3f-6686-4d4d-a7d7-9f681fba3170","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"4f378b3f-6686-4d4d-a7d7-9f681fba3170","chunk":"edited\nchanged lines: lines 6-8\n--- original\n+++ updated\n@@\n-## 2026-09-06\n-\n-### 2250 — v3 envelope owner named (terminalbackend), provider error lift built\n+## 2026-09-06\n+\n+### 2251 — review round 2: two wrapping bounds gates, fail-open lift arm, false-fact bound, blind census\n+\n+- SCOPE: TASK-260906-vmzk0y rework (F1–F5 blocking, F6–F7 notes). Production: `terminalbackend/descriptor.go` (early bound refusal in `descriptorGeometry`), `terminalbackend.go` (`semverMajor` saturates), `provhost/protocol.go` (`parseMajor` saturates, no new census branch), `provider/lift.go` (default arm fail-closed: unregistered → registry refusal, registered-no-arm → input handed back, never a wire object). Docs: provhost `doc.go`/`identity.go` bounds rewritten, descriptor future-caller paragraph. Tests: overflow vectors (F1/F2), registered-no-arm refusal (F4), §5.5 verify measurement + attestation tripwire (F3), whole-package multi-form derivation + 4 plants (F5), v3-error DecodeBound premise proof.\n+- FINDING (measured, not inferred): `VerifyObjectIdentity` on the pinned §5.5 example returns the claimed `record_id` with nil error — the example IS the true omit-self digest, so the old bound's justification was false; rewritten around the true deferral (admission contract includes non-recomputed digests; mismatched-live-binding ruling belongs to the identity owner). `VerifyObjectIdentity` has 0 production call sites repo-wide (AST scan over 125 files in `TestNoProductionPathAttestsProviderIdentityBinding`).\n+- FINDING: `provider` refusal inventory forbids `errors.New`/`fmt.Errorf`/`panic` outside `os_unix.go`/`os_windows.go`, so the F4 fix returns the input failure itself for registered-no-arm codes — no new construction site, audit untouched.\n+- FINDING: saturating (not unrecognizing) huge majors keeps the provhost parse-arm census stable (no new `return 0, false` branch) and routes 2^64+2 to `incompatible_protocol`/exit 6 instead of the exit-13 unusable-frame arm.\n+- EVIDENCE: outcome `TASK-260906-vmzk0y_outcome.md` updated on the board task (15/15 AC rows with call sites; battery 26 applied / 26 killed / 0 survivors + NOT_APPLIED and COMPILE_FAIL controls as distinct rows; candidate tree OID verified by `ls-tree`).\n+- GATES: `go test ./... -count=1` exit 0 (22 pkgs), `-race` on provider/provhost/terminalbackend exit 0, `-cover` exit 0 (provider 97.8%, provhost 85.8%, terminalbackend 94.2%), `go vet` + `GOOS=windows go vet` exit 0, gofmt clean, `go build` + `GOOS=windows go build` exit 0, catalog current, `tracecheck` ok (60 contracts, 98 acceptance cases).\n+- STATUS: Ready for review, handed off to review (review/integration are orchestrator steps).\n+\n+### 2250 — v3 envelope owner named (terminalbackend), provider error lift built\n"}}}
