T scan over 125 files in `TestNoProductionPathAttestsProviderIdentityBinding`).\n+- FINDING: `provider` refusal inventory forbids `errors.New`/`fmt.Errorf`/`panic` outside `os_unix.go`/`os_windows.go`, so the F4 fix returns the input failure itself for registered-no-arm codes — no new construction site, audit untouched.\n+- FINDING: saturating (not unrecognizing) huge majors keeps the provhost parse-arm census stable (no new `return 0, false` branch) and routes 2^64+2 to `incompatible_protocol`/exit 6 instead of the exit-13 unusable-frame arm.\n+- EVIDENCE: outcome `TASK-260906-vmzk0y_outcome.md` updated on the board task (15/15 AC rows with call sites; battery 26 applied / 26 killed / 0 survivors + NOT_APPLIED and COMPILE_FAIL controls as distinct rows; candidate tree OID verified by `ls-tree`).\n+- GATES: `go test ./... -count=1` exit 0 (22 pkgs), `-race` on provider/provhost/terminalbackend exit 0, `-cover` exit 0 (provider 97.8%, provhost 85.8%, terminalbackend 94.2%), `go vet` + `GOOS=windows go vet` exit 0, gofmt clean, `go build` + `GOOS=windows go build` exit 0, catalog current, `tracecheck` ok (60 contracts, 98 acceptance cases).\n+- STATUS: Ready for review, handed off to review (review/integration are orchestrator steps).\n+\n+### 2250 — v3 envelope owner named (terminalbackend), provider error lift built\n","edit_facts":{"tool_name":"edit_file","path":"LOGBOOK.md","added":13,"removed":3},"correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"edit_file","outcome":"success"}}}
